A #ponder("probability.random-variable")[random variable] on a probability space $(Omega, cal(F), PP)$ is a function $X: Omega -> RR$ such that
$
  {omega in Omega: X(omega) <= x} in cal(F) quad forall x in RR.
$
Write ${X <= x} = {omega in Omega: X(omega) <= x}$ and ${X in A} = {omega in Omega: X(omega) in A}$ for $A subset.eq RR$.
